  <section|Status><label|status>

  Draft, awaiting independent mathematical and source review. No Lean files
  were changed. Source revision is <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>
  from <verbatim|source/upstream.json>.

  Owned prose: <verbatim|manuscript/existence/annulus-two-wave-estimates.tex>.

  <section|Source declarations inspected><label|source-declarations-inspected>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><verbatim|YM.Stationary.polar_clock>, <verbatim|poleSpin>,
    <verbatim|absoluteGeode>, <verbatim|poleVec>, <verbatim|costZone>,
    <verbatim|polar_m>, <verbatim|peel_p>, <verbatim|joy_two>,
    <verbatim|joy_heights>: <verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/STATIONARY/OneLoop/MomentumIntegral.lean>.

    <item><verbatim|YM.Stationary.Waves1>, <verbatim|Waves2>,
    <verbatim|Rally>, <verbatim|Rally.coin>, <verbatim|Rally.register>,
    <verbatim|Rally.shell>, <verbatim|astronomy>:
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/STATIONARY/OneLoop/Bubbles.lean>.

    <item><verbatim|YM.Stationary.Fleet.bubbleHV>, <verbatim|bubbleControl>,
    <verbatim|tadControl>, <verbatim|haloControl>, <verbatim|rimEdge>,
    <verbatim|focus_bill>, <verbatim|ColdR>, <verbatim|Floe.vector>,
    <verbatim|Floe.ghost>, <verbatim|getReals>, <verbatim|haloRate>:
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/STATIONARY/OneLoop/Propagators.lean> and
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/STATIONARY/OneLoop/Bubbles.lean>.

    <item><verbatim|YM.Stationary.HorizCalc>,
    <verbatim|YM.Stationary.pouring>: <verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/STATIONARY/Level/Transition.lean>
    and <verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/STATIONARY/FullPlanned.lean>.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Expanded argument><label|expanded-argument>

  <\enumerate>
    <item><verbatim|polar_clock> identifies the coefficient functional
    <verbatim|alphaPay> of the analytically assembled response picture with
    the normalized integral of its continued second response kernel on the
    fundamental four-dimensional momentum region. This is not the finite
    sampled <verbatim|PoleTest> coefficient; the latter is the separate
    recording conclusion in <verbatim|HouseWord.done> and <verbatim|profit>.
    Differentiation under the integral is justified by the common analytic
    bound. <verbatim|poleSpin> then evaluates the continuum term: rotational
    invariance gives the angular moments <verbatim|1/4> and <verbatim|1/24>;
    the bracket has mean <verbatim|-11/12>; the radial integral of
    <verbatim|r^-4> over <verbatim|mu\<less\>r\<leq\>1> is <verbatim|2*pi^2
    log(mu^-1)>. With <verbatim|cartWeight=(2*pi)^-4>, this is exactly
    <verbatim|-11 Casimir/(24*pi^2) log(mu^-1)>, the source slope constant.

    <item>The finite two-channel identity is <verbatim|Rally.coin> together
    with <verbatim|haloRate>. The manuscript expands the free halo
    calculation, including <verbatim|tr(ad(e_b)^2)=-Casimir>: with
    <verbatim|rho=\|p\|^2>, <verbatim|C=-Casimir>, <verbatim|L=-4 p_1^2>, and
    <verbatim|Delta(t)=rho+2p_0 t+t^2>, the orbital and vector numerators are
    respectively <verbatim|LC/rho> and <verbatim|rho^{-1}(4L-8t^2)C>. The
    second numerator follows by multiplying the displayed 2-by-2 block
    matrices. Quotient differentiation gives their second derivatives, and
    orbital minus one half vector is <verbatim|2 poleVec>. The remaining
    interacting/reference split is exactly <verbatim|Rally.coin>; the factors
    <verbatim|1/2> arise from <verbatim|amena> and <verbatim|keelRay>.
    Subtracting the free halo identity yields the displayed
    response-minus-pole decomposition.

    <item><verbatim|Fleet.tadControl> gives the upper-channel bounds
    <verbatim|u/T^2+v*mu^2/T^6> (for each of the interacting and reference
    upper channels). <verbatim|Fleet.bubbleControl> bounds each whole lower
    face by <verbatim|A/T^4>; <verbatim|Fleet.haloControl> gives the
    lower-face errors after subtracting the corresponding free halos,
    <verbatim|A*(T+mu^2/T^2)/T^4> and <verbatim|B*(T+mu^2/T^2)/T^4>. Their
    proofs use <verbatim|Fiesta> product estimates and <verbatim|focus_bill>,
    whose trace step is <verbatim|\|\|trace M\|\| \<less\>= dim * vflux(M)>.
    In the astronomy application these are applied at two different scales:
    <verbatim|Rally.register> uses <verbatim|T1=\|x\|+mu> on all centered
    records, while <verbatim|Rally.shell> uses <verbatim|T2=\|x\|> only on
    the subfamily <verbatim|mu\<less\>=\|x\|>. The manuscript keeps these
    receipts separate. The local stationary-family proof that constructs
    their inputs is still an open prose-production obligation.

    <item>With <verbatim|T1=\|x\|+mu>, the full-frame identity gives the
    first wave <verbatim|\|g\|\<less\>=A1/T1^4>. At <verbatim|T2=\|x\|>,
    (AT5b) and the shell receipts give <verbatim|\|K-Pi\| \<less\>=
    (u+x0)/r^2+(v+y0)*mu^2/r^6 +(A+B)*(r^-3+mu^2*r^-6)>. Since
    <verbatim|r\<less\>=1>, this implies the second wave. Passing to real
    parts preserves the bound.

    <item>Lemma <verbatim|lem:path-radial-log> in
    <verbatim|path-attachment-producer.tex> integrates these two waves over
    the inner ball, annulus, and exterior of the unit ball. This unit proves
    the missing normalized pole identity and the finite-volume two-wave
    conversion; it does not claim a new bound on the local stationary chart's
    input price.
  </enumerate>

  <section|Exact scope and remaining dependencies><label|exact-scope-and-remaining-dependencies>

  The explicit finite-volume local receipts (all-centered whole-frame bound,
  shell upper/tadpole bounds, lower-face halo errors, and marked
  direction/color identities) are hypotheses of Proposition
  <verbatim|prop:ex-two-wave>. Their exact source conclusions are
  <verbatim|Rally.register>, <verbatim|Fleet.tadControl>,
  <verbatim|Fleet.haloControl>, and <verbatim|Rally.shell>; this unit proves
  the conversion of those conclusions to the radial bounds but does not
  reprove the local <verbatim|Hstar>/<verbatim|Orion>-to-<verbatim|Fleet>
  producer. <verbatim|astronomy> supplies the common quantifiers by applying
  the first estimate to all centered records and the second only to
  <verbatim|mu\<less\>=\|x\|>. <verbatim|pouring> additionally consumes the
  <verbatim|HouseWord.done>/<verbatim|massifTabs>/<verbatim|profit> finite
  recording chain and the <verbatim|absoluteGeode> invoice; the next owned
  unit traces those steps. This is not a proof of all upstream invoices or
  the public path recursion.

  <section|Checks actually run><label|checks-actually-run>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Targeted source declarations at the pinned revision were inspected;
    no Lean command was run.

    <item>No TeX build was run.

    <item><verbatim|python3 scripts/check_blueprint.py> was run and could not
    complete because the parent-owned <verbatim|blueprint/units/YM-000026/unit.json>
    is absent in this clone; no shared metadata file was created.

    <item><verbatim|git diff --no-index --check /dev/null FILE> was run for
    both owned files; it printed no whitespace diagnostics and returns status
    1 because each file is new relative to <verbatim|/dev/null>.
  </itemize-minus>

